Error [E0128]: A `Int` can't be used where a `CustomerID` is expected
  --> distinct_typed_head_from_int.jet:5:22
    |
  5 |     id :: CustomerID{n}
    |                      ^
 Why: `CustomerID` and `Int` are different types — even though `CustomerID` is built on `Int`, one is never accepted in place of the other
 Fix: Convert explicitly: `CustomerID.from_int(expr)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0128
